  "id": "Compound::DB01028 - Gene::2559",
  "verbalization": "Methoxyflurane is likely to interact with Gabra6 through a shared mechanism involving GABA receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Methoxyflurane binds to Gabra4 or Gabra2, which in turn participate in benzodiazepine receptor activity, ultimately leading to Gabra6's participation in this process. This implies a potential indirect interaction where Methoxyflurane may modulate GABA receptor function through these intermediate targets. The consistent involvement of Gabra6 in GABA receptor activity across different pathways supports a role in the overall effect of Methoxyflurane, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights a network of molecular interactions that may underlie the pharmacological effects of Methoxyflurane, with Gabra6 acting as a downstream effector in this pathway.",
